{{#if this.isVisible}}
    {{! Shade's `FormDescription` slot, in Ember's markup. The offer is a note
        about the input above it - what you can do now that the post is gated -
        so it goes where a note about that input goes, rather than becoming a
        second field competing with it.

        The link leads and the sentence explains it, rather than the other way
        round: the author is scanning the drawer, and the clickable words are
        what they're scanning for. }}
    <p class="gh-editor-access-hint">
        <button
            type="button"
            class="gh-editor-access-hint-link"
            data-test-button="add-free-preview"
            {{on "click" this.addFreePreview}}
        >Add a free preview</button> to show the start of this post to everyone, with a paywall to upgrade below it.
    </p>
{{/if}}
